ntributing\u002Freleases","9.contributing\u002F3.releases","i-lucide-rocket",{"title":213,"path":214,"stem":215,"icon":216},"Troubleshooting","\u002Ftroubleshooting","troubleshooting","i-lucide-life-buoy",{"id":218,"title":181,"body":219,"description":358,"extension":359,"links":360,"meta":361,"navigation":362,"path":182,"seo":363,"stem":183,"__hash__":364},"docs\u002F7.reference\u002F3.versioning.md",{"type":220,"value":221,"toc":352},"minimark",[222,226,231,247,250,308,311,322,326,329,347],[223,224,225],"p",{},"Prefer matching llama-crab package versions across Rust and TypeScript\nwhen one application uses more than one integration surface.",[227,228,230],"h2",{"id":229},"release-alignment","Release alignment",[223,232,233,234,238,239,242,243,246],{},"llama-crab keeps Rust crate releases and TypeScript package releases\naligned when public contracts change. The current workspace version is\n",[235,236,237],"code",{},"0.1.8"," (Rust crates and ",[235,240,241],{},"@llama-crab\u002Fcore"," \u002F ",[235,244,245],{},"@llama-crab\u002Ftauri"," are\nreleased together).",[223,248,249],{},"Notable cross-package guarantees and pin-level facts:",[251,252,253,264,281,297],"ul",{},[254,255,256,259,260,263],"li",{},[235,257,258],{},"Cargo.toml"," workspace ",[235,261,262],{},"version = \"0.1.8\"",". The same value drives the\nversion of every workspace crate.",[254,265,266,269,270,273,274,276,277,280],{},[235,267,268],{},"llama-crab"," and ",[235,271,272],{},"llama-crab-sys"," are published in lockstep as of\n",[235,275,237],{},", so consumers can pin ",[235,278,279],{},"llama-crab = \"0.1.8\""," and get the\nmatching FFI version automatically.",[254,282,283,269,285,287,288,290,291,293,294,296],{},[235,284,241],{},[235,286,245],{}," are at ",[235,289,237],{}," and depend\non each other at the same version (",[235,292,245],{}," depends on\n",[235,295,241],{},").",[254,298,299,300,303,304,307],{},"MSRV is ",[235,301,302],{},"1.88"," and is pinned in ",[235,305,306],{},"rust-toolchain.toml",". Bumping the\nMSRV is a breaking change and requires a major version bump.",[223,309,310],{},"For application upgrades:",[251,312,313,316,319],{},[254,314,315],{},"Upgrade related Rust crates and TypeScript packages together.",[254,317,318],{},"Read the generated Rust and TypeScript API references for changed\nsignatures.",[254,320,321],{},"Re-run the server, Tauri, embedding, reranking, or multimodal path\nyour app actually uses.",[227,323,325],{"id":324},"documentation-versioning","Documentation versioning",[223,327,328],{},"The Docusaurus site (this guide) initially publishes only the current\ndocumentation. Add Docusaurus versioned docs later if users need docs\nfor multiple released versions at the same time.",[223,330,331,332,335,336,339,340,346],{},"The previous GitHub Pages site under ",[235,333,334],{},"dominguesm.github.io\u002Fllama-crab\u002F","\nwas retired in release 0.1.5 — the docs\u002F folder and the\n",[235,337,338],{},"Publish docs site"," workflow have been removed from the source\nrepository, and all README files and crate-level docs now point at\n",[341,342,343],"a",{"href":343,"rel":344},"https:\u002F\u002Fllama-crab.nlp.rocks\u002F",[345],"nofollow",".",[223,348,349,350,346],{},"Release chores for maintainers are covered in\n",[341,351,208],{"href":209},{"title":353,"searchDepth":354,"depth":354,"links":355},"",2,[356,357],{"id":229,"depth":354,"text":230},{"id":324,"depth":354,"text":325},"Release alignment guidance for llama-crab packages and documentation.","md",null,{},{"icon":184},{"title":181,"description":358},"reQy81bC9Zy2f3eWd20yqSVRh4Mhc2bNiDPI8vZ_J1o",[366,368],{"title":176,"path":177,"stem":178,"description":367,"icon":179,"children":-1},"Feature flags for native backends and optional llama-crab capabilities.",{"title":186,"path":192,"stem":193,"description":369,"icon":187,"children":-1},"Runnable Rust and Tauri examples that cover every public feature of llama-crab 0.1.8.",1781622522936]